NOT COVERED BY THE LICENCE ABOVE
================================

This project depends on and refers to third party material. The following is a
statement of fact about what is here and what is not; it is not legal advice.

docs/BCD3000.PNG
    A manufacturer product photograph of the device, used to show which
    hardware this driver is for. It is not covered by the MIT licence above.
    It is embedded in the installer as a single, swappable resource so that it
    can be replaced with one file.

native/bcdasio/ (part of bcdasio.cpp)
    Part of the ASIO shell derives from Steinberg's ASIO SDK sample code,
    which carries the BSD 3-clause licence. That notice is reproduced in
    native/bcdasio/LICENSE-asiosample.txt and must be kept with any
    redistribution.

    The Steinberg ASIO SDK itself is NOT in this repository. The ASIO
    interface used by this driver is declared in native/bcdasio/asioapi.h,
    which is this project's own work, proved binary-identical to the SDK's
    declarations by the `abicheck` build target when the SDK is present on the
    building machine.

    "ASIO" is a trademark of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH. The ASIO logo
    is deliberately not used anywhere in this project.

teVirtualMIDI
    Copyright Tobias Erichsen. It is a RUN-TIME dependency: the control
    service loads teVirtualMIDI64.dll from the system directory to create one
    virtual MIDI port. It is NOT redistributed in this repository and NOT
    embedded in the installer. It reaches users through the author's own
    loopMIDI installer, from the author's own download page.

Behringer and BCD3000
    This is an independent, unofficial project with no affiliation with,
    endorsement by or connection to Behringer or Music Tribe. The device name
    is used only to identify which hardware this software works with. All
    trademarks belong to their owners.
